{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793668523615,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01G9toHNymaYfdQUTYTYa9JV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd crates/openfang-api/static/css; grep -n \"^\\.main-content\\|^\\.app-layout\\|^\\.stax-chips\\b\\|^\\.home \\|^\\.home-inner\\|^\\.home-head\\|^\\.sidebar[ {]\\|^\\.stax-dock[ {]\\|\\.page-body\\|^\\.sidebar\\b\" *.css | head -30; grep -n \"header-height\" theme.css"},"output":"components.css:1067:.sidebar-footer {\ncomponents.css:2366:.page-body { animation: slideIn 0.2s ease; }\nlayout.css:8:.app-layout {\nlayout.css:15:.sidebar {\nlayout.css:26:.sidebar.collapsed {\nlayout.css:30:.sidebar.collapsed .sidebar-label,\nlayout.css:31:.sidebar.collapsed .sidebar-header-text,\nlayout.css:32:.sidebar.collapsed .nav-label { display: none; }\nlayout.css:34:.sidebar.collapsed .nav-item { justify-content: center; padding: 12px 0; }\nlayout.css:36:.sidebar-header {\nlayout.css:45:.sidebar-logo {\nlayout.css:51:.sidebar-logo img {\nlayout.css:58:.sidebar-logo img:hover {\nlayout.css:68:.sidebar-header h1 {\nlayout.css:76:.sidebar-header .version {\nlayout.css:83:.sidebar-status {\nlayout.css:93:.sidebar-status.offline { color: var(--error); }\nlayout.css:115:.sidebar-nav {\nlayout.css:121:.sidebar-nav::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 0; }\nlayout.css:136:.sidebar.collapsed .nav-section-title { display: none; }\nlayout.css:188:.sidebar-toggle {\nlayout.css:198:.sidebar-toggle:hover { color: var(--text); }\nlayout.css:201:.main-content {\nlayout.css:211:   and be flex containers so .page-body can scroll. */\nlayout.css:212:.main-content > div {\nlayout.css:236:.page-body {\nlayout.css:244:.sidebar-overlay {\nlayout.css:271:  .page-body { padding: 16px; }\nlayout.css:312:  .page-body { padding: 12px; }\nlayout.css:334:.app-layout.focus-mode .sidebar { display: none; }\n58:  --header-height: 52px;\n","metadata":{"output":"components.css:1067:.sidebar-footer {\ncomponents.css:2366:.page-body { animation: slideIn 0.2s ease; }\nlayout.css:8:.app-layout {\nlayout.css:15:.sidebar {\nlayout.css:26:.sidebar.collapsed {\nlayout.css:30:.sidebar.collapsed .sidebar-label,\nlayout.css:31:.sidebar.collapsed .sidebar-header-text,\nlayout.css:32:.sidebar.collapsed .nav-label { display: none; }\nlayout.css:34:.sidebar.collapsed .nav-item { justify-content: center; padding: 12px 0; }\nlayout.css:36:.sidebar-header {\nlayout.css:45:.sidebar-logo {\nlayout.css:51:.sidebar-logo img {\nlayout.css:58:.sidebar-logo img:hover {\nlayout.css:68:.sidebar-header h1 {\nlayout.css:76:.sidebar-header .version {\nlayout.css:83:.sidebar-status {\nlayout.css:93:.sidebar-status.offline { color: var(--error); }\nlayout.css:115:.sidebar-nav {\nlayout.css:121:.sidebar-nav::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 0; }\nlayout.css:136:.sidebar.collapsed .nav-section-title { display: none; }\nlayout.css:188:.sidebar-toggle {\nlayout.css:198:.sidebar-toggle:hover { color: var(--text); }\nlayout.css:201:.main-content {\nlayout.css:211:   and be flex containers so .page-body can scroll. */\nlayout.css:212:.main-content > div {\nlayout.css:236:.page-body {\nlayout.css:244:.sidebar-overlay {\nlayout.css:271:  .page-body { padding: 16px; }\nlayout.css:312:  .page-body { padding: 12px; }\nlayout.css:334:.app-layout.focus-mode .sidebar { display: none; }\n58:  --header-height: 52px;\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd crates/openfang-api/static/css; grep -n \"^\\.main-content\\|^\\.app-layout\\|^\\.stax-chips\\b\\|^\\.home \\|^\\.home-inner\\|^\\.home-head\\|^\\.sidebar[ {]\\|^\\.stax-dock[ {]\\|\\.page-body\\|^\\.sidebar\\b\" *.css | head -30; grep -n \"header-height\" theme.css","time":{"start":1793668523566,"end":1793668523612}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I realize the drawer and backdrop sit above the hamburger button in stacking order, so tapping it again while open wouldn't register — I need the hamburger itself to float above the scrim when the drawer is open so it stays tappable to close.\n\nAnother option: the page content pushes right instead of the drawer overlaying, Slack/Discord-style, so the hamburger shifts with the page and remains visible in the exposed strip — though at 390px width that strip is barely wide enough to keep it visible.\n\nMaybe simpler to just keep the hamburger fixed and elevated above the drawer, having the drawer header shift its brand mark over to make room for it in the same spot.\n\nBut I notice the hamburger sits at slightly different coordinates across surfaces, so I'm considering a shell-level toggle: measure the exact bounding rect of whichever hamburger opened the drawer, then render a floating twin at that precise position, layered above the drawer itself.\n\nFor edge-swipe opens with no originating button, I'd fall back to whatever `.stax-menu-btn` is currently visible, or a default position if none exist. I'm also weighing whether it's simpler to just bump the real hamburger buttons' z-index above the drawer, depending on whether their containers already form stacking contexts.\n\nChecking positions though, the hamburger's horizontal placement differs across home-head versus chips versus the drawer header padding — they'd overlap rather than align cleanly, so this needs more adjustment.\n\nBut I also need to verify which surfaces actually show the hamburger versus relying on edge-swipe alone, since forms and SMS pages apparently lack the button entirely based on the grep results.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19ef9a4bc001Gr42dT7cWXEciz","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19ef942af001k1YvOBei2odqNs"}}
