.png\nphone-dark-2-drawer-open.png\nphone-dark-3-drawer-expanded.png\nphone-dark-4-settings.png\nphone-dark-5-connections.png\nphone-dark-6-advanced.png\nphone-dark-7-advanced-settings-console-providers.png\nphone-dark-8-advanced-integrations.png\nphone-dark-9-advanced-helpers.png\nphone-light-10-ask-stax-drafted.png\nphone-light-1-dock-home.png\nphone-light-2-drawer-open.png\nphone-light-3-drawer-expanded.png\nphone-light-4-settings.png\nphone-light-5-connections.png\nphone-light-6-advanced.png\nphone-light-7-advanced-settings-console-providers.png\nphone-light-8-advanced-integrations.png\nphone-light-9-advanced-helpers.png\nsetup-0-integrations-signal-saved.png\n","metadata":{"output":"#!/bin/bash\nIFS= read -r K\nexport OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$K\"\ncd ~/openfang-build/repo || exit 1\nsetsid nohup ~/.local/bin/opencode run --auto --format json -m openrouter/anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 \"Implement ROUND3-BRIEF.md exactly. Part A - drawer gestures: remove the X from the drawer header (brand and wordmark only); the hamburger button toggles the drawer open AND closed from every surface that shows it; a drag starting in a ~24px left-edge grab zone pulls the card out following the finger, releasing past ~40 percent of card width or with a flick opens it, releasing earlier snaps shut; with the card open, dragging the card or the scrim leftward follows the finger and closes past the same threshold, a quick leftward swipe closes outright, scrim tap still closes; Pointer Events and transforms only; never hijack vertical scrolling or drags beginning on interactive elements outside the edge zone; ESC closes on desktop; prefers-reduced-motion falls back to the plain toggle with no follow-drag; drawer internals unchanged (one scroll container, sections start closed, OWNER block in flow, no tiles strip). Part B - the grim reaper is the brand: consume the staged assets at ~/openfang-build/icon-assets/reaper/ as-is and never redraw the character: stax-avatar.svg replaces the arrow in the drawer brand tile, the Home header avatar, the TEAM Stax row, the Stax card, and the dock Stax icon; the Home centerpiece becomes the mascot large and centered - ship stax-mascot-phone.png if it holds up at ~180px, else stax-mascot-idle.jpg, and report which; the sign-in screen brand mark becomes the reaper; point the favicon at the reaper avatar too if it is a static asset and report it; the circular-arrow mark leaves owner surfaces (asset files stay in the tree untouched) - report what you did with it. Do NOT redraw any other icon this round (Work, Boards, Leads, Channels and the drawer rows stay exactly as Round 2 left them). Presentation layer only: crates/openfang-api/static/** plus webchat.rs include_str! lines if a new static asset must be served; no server routes, no kernel/hand/sidecar changes. Then run the brief gate on the final binary in staging (390x844 and desktop, dark and light): exercise every gesture your harness can drive and state plainly which it cannot; a markup scan proving no X in the drawer; branding captures (sign-in, Home with mascot centerpiece, drawer brand tile and TEAM row, Stax card, dock) with the reaper present and the arrow absent; non-regression checks (sections closed at open, Settings plain list, System module dock, vocabulary scans, zero console errors). The release build must pass. Two local commits on stax-ux, one per part. Build and stage only - no deploy, no git push.\" -f ~/openfang-build/ROUND3-BRIEF.md > ~/openfang-build/round3-run.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &\necho \"LAUNCHED pid=$!\"\n----\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1793666511655,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e613e3359ffexqBtPTL7r1h7kJ\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"toolu_01URBArrfWYFANq6uW2UFD9N\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"B0=/home/shawnlowe/openfang-build/repo/target/release/openfang; B=/tmp/opencode/c2\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1793666511675,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e613e3359ffexqBtPTL7r1h7kJ\