{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793668801554,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01FVNTkQc9bB35uf6F25ZrpF","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd crates/openfang-api/static && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='index_body.html'; s=open(p).read()\nold_a='''        <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = true\" aria-label=\"Open menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nnew_a='''        <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = !$store.app.sideOpen\" :aria-expanded=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 'true' : 'false'\" aria-controls=\"stax-side\" aria-label=\"Menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nassert s.count(old_a)==1; s=s.replace(old_a,new_a)\nold_b='''            <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" x-show=\"surf() !== 'channels'\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = true\" aria-label=\"Open menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nnew_b='''            <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" x-show=\"surf() !== 'channels'\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = !$store.app.sideOpen\" :aria-expanded=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 'true' : 'false'\" aria-controls=\"stax-side\" aria-label=\"Menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nassert s.count(old_b)==1; s=s.replace(old_b,new_b)\nold_c='''<!-- Side card — opened from the shell bar's menu button. One composition:\n     wordmark, the team as people, the app's places, Stax conversations,\n     owner block — one scroll. Every row is a projection of real state and opens an\n     existing page key; navigating anywhere closes the drawer (navigate()). -->\n<div class=\"stax-side-backdrop\" x-show=\"$store.app.sideOpen\" x-cloak @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\"></div>\n<aside class=\"stax-side\" :class=\"{ open: $store.app.sideOpen }\" :inert=\"!$store.app.sideOpen\" x-data=\"staxDrawer()\" x-init=\"initDrawer()\" @keydown.escape.window=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\" aria-label=\"Menu\">'''\nnew_c='''<!-- Side card — the menu button toggles it; it also follows a drag from the\n     left screen edge, and a leftward drag on the card or the dimmed page\n     closes it (gestures in staxDrawer().initGestures, app.js). One composition:\n     wordmark, the team as people, the app's places, Stax conversations,\n     owner block — one scroll. Every row is a projection of real state and opens an\n     existing page key; navigating anywhere closes the drawer (navigate()). -->\n<div class=\"stax-side-backdrop sd-scrim\" x-cloak :class=\"{ 'is-open': $store.app.sideOpen }\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\"></div>\n<!-- The menu button, held above the open card at the spot it was tapped,\n     so the same three lines close what they opened. -->\n<button class=\"stax-menu-btn sd-toggle\" x-cloak :class=\"{ 'is-open': $store.app.sideOpen }\" :tabindex=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 0 : -1\" :aria-hidden=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 'false' : 'true'\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = !$store.app.sideOpen\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"stax-side\" aria-label=\"Menu\" title=\"Menu\">\n  <svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16\"/></svg>\n</button>\n<aside class=\"stax-side\" id=\"stax-side\" :class=\"{ open: $store.app.sideOpen }\" :inert=\"!$store.app.sideOpen\" x-data=\"staxDrawer()\" x-init=\"initDrawer()\" @keydown.escape.window=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\" aria-label=\"Menu\">'''\nassert s.count(old_c)==1; s=s.replace(old_c,new_c)\nold_d='''    <button class=\"sd-close\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\" aria-label=\"Close menu\"><svg class=\"sd-ico\"><use href=\"#g-close\"/></svg></button>\n'''\nassert s.count(old_d)==1; s=s.replace(old_d,'')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"g-close\\|sd-close\" index_body.html css/*.css js/*.js"},"output":"index_body.html:38:    <symbol id=\"g-close\" viewBox=\"8 8 48 48\"><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"4\"><path d=\"M20 20 L44 44 M44 20 L20 44\"/></g></symbol>\ncss/layout.css:426:.sd-close { margin-left: auto; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 44px; height: 44px; border: none; background: none; border-radius: 10px; color: var(--text-dim); cursor: pointer; }\ncss/layout.css:427:.sd-close:hover { background: var(--sd-hover); color: var(--text); }\n","metadata":{"output":"index_body.html:38:    <symbol id=\"g-close\" viewBox=\"8 8 48 48\"><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"4\"><path d=\"M20 20 L44 44 M44 20 L20 44\"/></g></symbol>\ncss/layout.css:426:.sd-close { margin-left: auto; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 44px; height: 44px; border: none; background: none; border-radius: 10px; color: var(--text-dim); cursor: pointer; }\ncss/layout.css:427:.sd-close:hover { background: var(--sd-hover); color: var(--text); }\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd crates/openfang-api/static && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='index_body.html'; s=open(p).read()\nold_a='''        <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = true\" aria-label=\"Open menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nnew_a='''        <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = !$store.app.sideOpen\" :aria-expanded=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 'true' : 'false'\" aria-controls=\"stax-side\" aria-label=\"Menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nassert s.count(old_a)==1; s=s.replace(old_a,new_a)\nold_b='''            <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" x-show=\"surf() !== 'channels'\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = true\" aria-label=\"Open menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nnew_b='''            <button class=\"stax-menu-btn\" x-show=\"surf() !== 'channels'\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = !$store.app.sideOpen\" :aria-expanded=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 'true' : 'false'\" aria-controls=\"stax-side\" aria-label=\"Menu\" title=\"Menu\">'''\nassert s.count(old_b)==1; s=s.replace(old_b,new_b)\nold_c='''<!-- Side card — opened from the shell bar's menu button. One composition:\n     wordmark, the team as people, the app's places, Stax conversations,\n     owner block — one scroll. Every row is a projection of real state and opens an\n     existing page key; navigating anywhere closes the drawer (navigate()). -->\n<div class=\"stax-side-backdrop\" x-show=\"$store.app.sideOpen\" x-cloak @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\"></div>\n<aside class=\"stax-side\" :class=\"{ open: $store.app.sideOpen }\" :inert=\"!$store.app.sideOpen\" x-data=\"staxDrawer()\" x-init=\"initDrawer()\" @keydown.escape.window=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\" aria-label=\"Menu\">'''\nnew_c='''<!-- Side card — the menu button toggles it; it also follows a drag from the\n     left screen edge, and a leftward drag on the card or the dimmed page\n     closes it (gestures in staxDrawer().initGestures, app.js). One composition:\n     wordmark, the team as people, the app's places, Stax conversations,\n     owner block — one scroll. Every row is a projection of real state and opens an\n     existing page key; navigating anywhere closes the drawer (navigate()). -->\n<div class=\"stax-side-backdrop sd-scrim\" x-cloak :class=\"{ 'is-open': $store.app.sideOpen }\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\"></div>\n<!-- The menu button, held above the open card at the spot it was tapped,\n     so the same three lines close what they opened. -->\n<button class=\"stax-menu-btn sd-toggle\" x-cloak :class=\"{ 'is-open': $store.app.sideOpen }\" :tabindex=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 0 : -1\" :aria-hidden=\"$store.app.sideOpen ? 'false' : 'true'\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = !$store.app.sideOpen\" aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-controls=\"stax-side\" aria-label=\"Menu\" title=\"Menu\">\n  <svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16\"/></svg>\n</button>\n<aside class=\"stax-side\" id=\"stax-side\" :class=\"{ open: $store.app.sideOpen }\" :inert=\"!$store.app.sideOpen\" x-data=\"staxDrawer()\" x-init=\"initDrawer()\" @keydown.escape.window=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\" aria-label=\"Menu\">'''\nassert s.count(old_c)==1; s=s.replace(old_c,new_c)\nold_d='''    <button class=\"sd-close\" @click=\"$store.app.sideOpen = false\" aria-label=\"Close menu\"><svg class=\"sd-ico\"><use href=\"#g-close\"/></svg></button>\n'''\nassert s.count(old_d)==1; s=s.replace(old_d,'')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"g-close\\|sd-close\" index_body.html css/*.css js/*.js","time":{"start":1793668801474,"end":1793668801550}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm deciding to add a fixed-position twin hamburger button that covers both phone and desktop placements, since on phone it would overlap the real one anyway since it's hidden under the card.\n\nI'm working through the header padding math so the twin button and brand tile align, and confirming the twin's visibility should toggle with drag progress and open state rather than being tied to the aside itself—keeping it fixed so the card slides underneath it naturally, which also handles the desktop case where the page's own hamburger gets covered by the drawer.\n\nI'm also adding ARIA attributes to the toggle buttons and twin close button for accessibility, and reworking the scrim from x-show to an always-rendered element with opacity/visibility transitions so drag gestures can animate it smoothly with inline styles overriding the CSS transition during drag.\n\nNow I'm writing the gesture-handling function for the drawer, setting up edge-swipe detection thresholds and references to the scrim and toggle elements...\n\nStill writing drag handlers...\n\nWriting pointer move handler...\n\nI'm capturing the pointer to the right element to suppress stray clicks, then computing drag progress as a clamped ratio of displacement to width depending on open/close mode, sampling recent movement for velocity, and scheduling paint updates via requestAnimationFrame while considering how to block scroll on touch.\n\nSince our slop threshold of 10 is smaller than Chrome's own ~15, we're deciding to engage before Chrome starts its native scroll, but if vertical movement dominates we abandon and let native scrolling take over. Touch-action settings differ by mode: pan-y for the aside in close mode, none for the scrim, and auto for content in the edge zone where we rely on non-passive preventDefault. I'm also considering that CDP-driven touch dispatch generates real touch and pointer events, giving us a genuine test path through the harness.\n\nWriting pointer-up handler...\n\nThe release logic computes velocity from recent samples and decides the final open/closed state based on either a flick threshold or how far past the midpoint the drag ended, then calls finish() to lock in that state and suppress the resulting click. On cancel, I snap back to whatever state we started in rather than computing a new decision. The finish() function clears inline styles and updates the store, and I'm working through how the transition animates from the last painted inline value now that the transition property is restored.\n\nShort swipes under the slop threshold shouldn't count, so flick requires enough engagement distance. For scrim taps, I need to suppress the click event right after a drag ends so it doesn't also trigger a close — I'll add a temporary capturing click listener that blocks and removes itself shortly after.\n\nI'm also second-guessing the `inert` attribute on the aside while it's closed: if inert elements don't receive pointer events, then during an open-drag gesture starting from the edge, the hit-testing might behave unexpectedly since the aside itself is inert at that moment.\n\nSince events will still reach the window listeners either way, I don't think pointer capture is necessary here, since touch already gets implicit capture and mouse works fine with window-level listeners. I'm now sketching a touchmove blocker that prevents default scrolling while a drag gesture is actively engaged.\n\nMy concern is timing: our drag engages at 10px of movement, while Chrome's native scroll slop is roughly 15dip, so our preventDefault should always fire before Chrome would try to start scrolling on its own. Pointermove events fire throughout this slop zone, and Chrome only cancels the pointer sequence if the touchmove wasn't already prevented, so the ordering should work out correctly.\n\nI should also set `touch-action: pan-y` on the aside so horizontal drags there don't trigger native panning and keep pointer events flowing, with the scrim using `touch-action: none`. I need to account for the edge zone interacting with `overscroll-behavior` and Android's back-gesture, and the drawer width being `min(360px, 88vw)` so the 40% threshold is relative to that. Reduced-motion users should skip the follow-drag behavior entirely since CSS already disables transitions, and I need to watch for conflicts with the horizontally-scrollable chip row near the edge, where a rightward drag could be ambiguous between opening the drawer and scrolling the chips.\n\nThinking about text inputs inside the edge zone — I'm debating whether to exclude interactive elements like inputs, textareas, and contenteditable fields from triggering the drawer drag, since a user starting a drag there likely wants to select text rather than open the sidebar.\n\nI should also handle edge cases: dock buttons spanning the edge zone, chat row buttons during close-mode drags, vertical scroll detection to abandon the gesture in favor of native scrolling, keeping the existing escape-key handler, and canceling an in-progress drag if the sidebar state changes programmatically mid-gesture.\n\nNow I'm moving to the shell-level hamburger toggle and writing the CSS transitions for the scrim overlay, fading opacity and visibility with a custom easing curve.\n\nWriting scrim transition styles...\n\nStill writing drawer styles...\n\nNow I'm checking positioning math for the hamburger and chips on phone layout, making sure the twin menu button aligns at the right offsets against the drawer header.\n\nI also want to handle focus management: if the user opened the drawer via keyboard on the page hamburger, I should move focus to the twin button so Enter toggles close, and on close return focus appropriately rather than leaving it stuck on a covered element.\n\nNow I'll move on to writing the HTML edits.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19efdc10c001jOmWGy0NiWNk1u","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19efcc5920010ye1rJ3BnrJ7nZ"}}
