{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793668909524,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"id":"prt_19eff89cd001Bblz4HcLU1eh5l","messageID":"msg_19eff64f3001wAP7hm588ljaRa","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","snapshot":"39b5b29738210a217e0a096d94cdd2b5a6810450","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793668939401,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"toolu_01Jsn8Q9BL8sZrps1kz4UUxL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import json, sys\nbase, cfg, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3]\nphone = cfg.startswith('phone')\nw, h = (390, 844) if phone else (1440, 900)\ndark = 'dark' in cfg\nreduce = 'reduce' in cfg\nkind = 'touch' if phone else 'mouse'\nST = \"(()=>{const s=document.querySelector('.stax-side');const sc=document.querySelector('.sd-scrim');const t=document.querySelector('.sd-toggle');const r=s.getBoundingClientRect();return {open:s.classList.contains('open'),store:Alpine.store('app').sideOpen,cardLeft:Math.round(r.left),cardW:Math.round(r.width),scrim:getComputedStyle(sc).opacity,toggleVis:getComputedStyle(t).visibility,dragging:s.classList.contains('is-dragging'),secsOpen:[...s.querySelectorAll('.sd-sec-head')].filter(x=>x.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true').length}})()\"\nMENU = \"(()=>{const b=[...document.querySelectorAll('.stax-menu-btn:not(.sd-toggle)')].find(b=>b.offsetParent);const r=b.getBoundingClientRect();return [Math.round(r.left+r.width/2),Math.round(r.top+r.height/2)]})()\"\nCLOSE = \"(()=>{Alpine.store('app').sideOpen=false;return 1})()\"\nOPEN = \"(()=>{Alpine.store('app').sideOpen=true;return 1})()\"\nW = min(360, round(w * 0.88))\ny = 420\nsteps = [\n  {\"nav\": base + \"/\", \"ms\": 3000},\n  {\"eval\": \"localStorage.setItem('openfang-theme-mode','%s')\" % ('dark' if dark else 'light')},\n  {\"eval\": \"(async()=>{const p=document.querySelector('input[type=password]');if(p&&p.offsetParent){await Alpine.store('app').sessionLogin('admin','selfcheck-pw');}return Alpine.store('app').sessionUser})()\", \"wait\": 1200},\n  {\"nav\": \"about:blank\", \"ms\": 300}, {\"nav\": base + \"/#chat\", \"ms\": 4000},\n  {\"label\": \"markup: X in drawer?\", \"eval\": \"(()=>{const s=document.querySelector('.stax-side');return {closeBtns:s.querySelectorAll('.sd-close,[aria-label*=Close i],use[href=\\\"#g-close\\\"]').length,gCloseSymbol:!!document.getElementById('g-close'),xGlyphText:/[\\\\u00d7\\\\u2715\\\\u2716\\\\u2717]/.test(s.innerHTML),headButtons:s.querySelectorAll('.sd-head button').length,headText:s.querySelector('.sd-head').innerText.replace(/\\\\n/g,' | ')}})()\"},\n  {\"label\": \"start\", \"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"menu button center\", \"eval\": MENU},\n]\nmx, my = (26, 26)  # replaced at runtime by eval? keep fixed slot; verified via MENU output\nsteps += [\n  {\"label\": \"hamburger tap opens\", \"eval\": \"(()=>{window.__m=\" + MENU + \";return window.__m})()\"},\n]\nimport itertools\ndef tapmenu():\n    return {\"eval\": \"(()=>{const b=document.elementFromPoint(window.__m[0],window.__m[1]);b.closest('button').click();return b.closest('button').className})()\", \"wait\": 500}\nsteps += [tapmenu(), {\"eval\": ST}, {\"shot\": out + \"/\" + cfg + \"-a1-menu-open.png\"},\n          {\"label\": \"hamburger (same spot) closes\", **tapmenu()}, {\"eval\": ST}]\nif phone:\n    steps += [\n      {\"label\": \"real touch tap on menu opens\", \"eval\": \"1\"}, {\"tap\": {\"x\": 28, \"y\": 26}, \"wait\": 600}, {\"eval\": ST},\n      {\"label\": \"real touch tap same spot closes\", \"eval\": \"1\"}, {\"tap\": {\"x\": 28, \"y\": 26}, \"wait\": 600}, {\"eval\": ST},\n    ]\nsteps += [\n  {\"label\": \"edge drag 25% then release slowly -> snaps shut\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": 4, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": 4 + W * 0.25, \"y1\": y + 6, \"n\": 14, \"ms\": 700, \"hold\": 250, \"kind\": kind, \"shotAt\": 14, \"shot\": out + \"/\" + cfg + \"-a2-mid-drag-25.png\", \"probe\": ST}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"edge drag 60% slow -> opens\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": 4, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": 4 + W * 0.6, \"y1\": y - 8, \"n\": 16, \"ms\": 800, \"hold\": 250, \"kind\": kind, \"shotAt\": 10, \"shot\": out + \"/\" + cfg + \"-a3-mid-drag-open.png\", \"probe\": ST}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST}, {\"shot\": out + \"/\" + cfg + \"-a4-after-edge-open.png\"},\n  {\"label\": \"card drag left 20% slow -> stays open\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": W * 0.7, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": W * 0.5, \"y1\": y, \"n\": 10, \"ms\": 600, \"hold\": 250, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"card drag left 55% slow -> closes\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": W * 0.8, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": W * 0.25, \"y1\": y + 4, \"n\": 14, \"ms\": 700, \"hold\": 250, \"kind\": kind, \"shotAt\": 8, \"shot\": out + \"/\" + cfg + \"-a5-mid-drag-close.png\", \"probe\": ST}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"edge flick (short, fast) -> opens\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": 4, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": 70, \"y1\": y, \"n\": 4, \"ms\": 50, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"quick leftward swipe on card -> closes\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": W * 0.6, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": W * 0.45, \"y1\": y, \"n\": 3, \"ms\": 45, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"eval\": OPEN, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"label\": \"drag on dimmed page leftward -> closes\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": W + (w - W) * 0.5, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": W * 0.35, \"y1\": y, \"n\": 14, \"ms\": 700, \"hold\": 250, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"eval\": OPEN, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"label\": \"tap dimmed page -> closes\", \"tap\": {\"x\": round(W + (w - W) * 0.5), \"y\": y, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"drag starting outside the edge zone (x=60) -> stays closed\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": 60, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": 60 + W * 0.7, \"y1\": y, \"n\": 14, \"ms\": 600, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"vertical drag from edge zone -> stays closed\", \"drag\": {\"x0\": 6, \"y0\": 650, \"x1\": 12, \"y1\": 250, \"n\": 12, \"ms\": 500, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"vertical scroll inside open card still scrolls (sections expanded)\", \"eval\": \"(async()=>{Alpine.store('app').sideOpen=true;await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,500));for(const hh of document.querySelectorAll('.sd-sec-head'))hh.click();await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,300));const b=document.querySelector('.sd-body');return {scrollH:b.scrollHeight,clientH:b.clientHeight,top:b.scrollTop}})()\"},\n  {\"drag\": {\"x0\": W * 0.5, \"y0\": 700, \"x1\": W * 0.52, \"y1\": 300, \"n\": 12, \"ms\": 400, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 800},\n  {\"eval\": \"(()=>({top:document.querySelector('.sd-body').scrollTop, open:Alpine.store('app').sideOpen}))()\"},\n  {\"label\": \"re-open after closing: sections closed again\", \"eval\": CLOSE, \"wait\": 500},\n  {\"drag\": {\"x0\": 4, \"y0\": y, \"x1\": 4 + W * 0.7, \"y1\": y, \"n\": 14, \"ms\": 600, \"hold\": 200, \"kind\": kind}, \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n  {\"label\": \"Esc closes\", \"key\": \"Escape\", \"wait\": 600},\n  {\"eval\": ST},\n]\njson.dump({\"width\": w, \"height\": h, \"mobile\": phone, \"touch\": phone, \"dark\": dark, \"reduce\": reduce, \"steps\": steps}, open('/tmp/opencode/r3/gest-' + cfg + '.json', 'w'))\n","filePath":"/tmp/opencode/r3/gest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/tmp/opencode/r3/gest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"../../../../tmp/opencode/r3/gest.py","time":{"start":1793668939386,"end":1793668939395}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm sketching a gesture test spec generator that logs in, probes sidebar state (open flag, store value, transform, scrim opacity), and verifies tapping the hamburger button toggles the menu open then closed by tapping the same coordinates twice, followed by edge-drag interaction checks.\n\nI'm continuing to define more drag scenarios: partial slow edge drags that close or open the drawer depending on threshold, a swipe-left flick to close an open card, slow partial drags that either keep the card open or close it past a percentage threshold, scrim dragging and tapping to close, and finally a vertical scroll test from the edge to confirm the drawer stays closed while checking if scroll position changes inside a scrollable area like settings or the drawer body.\n\nI'm also outlining edge cases: drags starting outside the edge zone that shouldn't open the drawer, a fast flick that should open it, ESC key closing on desktop, a reduced-motion variant where the drawer stays closed below a threshold, and a mouse-based drag variant for desktop testing. I'm noting the probe expression needs to return both the open state and the transform value.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19effab1a001ZEm1yJWCSWjKkW","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19eff64f3001wAP7hm588ljaRa"}}
