.json 2>&1 | grep eval","time":{"start":1793668992537,"end":1793668997517}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The console errors seem tied to the proxy setup rather than real issues, so I should verify against the actual binary later. Most of the results look fine, but the edge flick gesture—a short, fast swipe—didn't trigger as expected; I'm checking the timing of the dispatched move events to see if the velocity calculation is being affected by how CDP coalesces timestamps during the sleep intervals between steps.\n\nI'm wondering if pointer events get aligned to animation frames, which could explain why engagement triggers on a later move than expected rather than the first one. The swipe-to-close test may have been meaningless since the card was already closed from the failed flick, so that particular pass doesn't confirm anything; separately, there's an uncaught error during one of the drag evaluations that I need to trace back to its source.\n\nActually, I suspect the rightward drag at x=60 triggered Chrome's overscroll history navigation gesture, sending the page back to about:blank and breaking Alpine — which would explain the \"Uncaught\" error. Since our edge-drag handler calls preventDefault on touchmove, that should already guard against this for our intended interactions, but for testing I should disable the overscroll navigation feature flag and add instrumentation to log pointer events during the flick to debug further.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19f00cb23001OPkYTOOvtM3dQr","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19f009165001vGpoWQpXUsvvLG"}}
