{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793669039410,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_01EZdmAfmXWNsfQeGhW7Vvpx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd ~/openfang-build/repo/crates/openfang-api/static/js && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='app.js'; s=open(p).read()\nold=s[s.index('      function velocity(samples) {'):s.index('      // A drag that ends over a row')]\nnew='''      // Speed over the last ~100ms of movement, in px/ms. A finger that\n      // rested before lifting has no speed left.\n      function velocity(samples, upAt) {\n        var last = samples[samples.length - 1];\n        if (upAt - last[0] > 120) return 0;\n        var first = last;\n        for (var i = samples.length - 2; i >= 0; i--) {\n          if (last[0] - samples[i][0] > 100) break;\n          first = samples[i];\n        }\n        var dt = last[0] - first[0];\n        return dt > 0 ? (last[1] - first[1]) / dt : 0;\n      }\n'''\ns=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace('''        was.samples.push([e.timeStamp, e.clientX]);\n        var v = velocity(was.samples);''','''        var v = velocity(was.samples, e.timeStamp);''')\ns=s.replace(\"var EDGE = 24, SLOP = 10, THRESHOLD = 0.4, FLICK = 0.45; // FLICK in px/ms\",\"var EDGE = 24, SLOP = 10, THRESHOLD = 0.4, FLICK = 0.3; // FLICK in px/ms\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"FLICK = \\|velocity(was\" app.js"},"output":"877:      var EDGE = 24, SLOP = 10, THRESHOLD = 0.4, FLICK = 0.3; // FLICK in px/ms\n972:        var v = velocity(was.samples, e.timeStamp);\n","metadata":{"output":"877:      var EDGE = 24, SLOP = 10, THRESHOLD = 0.4, FLICK = 0.3; // FLICK in px/ms\n972:        var v = velocity(was.samples, e.timeStamp);\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/openfang-build/repo/crates/openfang-api/static/js && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='app.js'; s=open(p).read()\nold=s[s.index('      function velocity(samples) {'):s.index('      // A drag that ends over a row')]\nnew='''      // Speed over the last ~100ms of movement, in px/ms. A finger that\n      // rested before lifting has no speed left.\n      function velocity(samples, upAt) {\n        var last = samples[samples.length - 1];\n        if (upAt - last[0] > 120) return 0;\n        var first = last;\n        for (var i = samples.length - 2; i >= 0; i--) {\n          if (last[0] - samples[i][0] > 100) break;\n          first = samples[i];\n        }\n        var dt = last[0] - first[0];\n        return dt > 0 ? (last[1] - first[1]) / dt : 0;\n      }\n'''\ns=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace('''        was.samples.push([e.timeStamp, e.clientX]);\n        var v = velocity(was.samples);''','''        var v = velocity(was.samples, e.timeStamp);''')\ns=s.replace(\"var EDGE = 24, SLOP = 10, THRESHOLD = 0.4, FLICK = 0.45; // FLICK in px/ms\",\"var EDGE = 24, SLOP = 10, THRESHOLD = 0.4, FLICK = 0.3; // FLICK in px/ms\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"FLICK = \\|velocity(was\" app.js","time":{"start":1793669039355,"end":1793669039407}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking the event handling and velocity calculation—looking at timestamp intervals within a 90ms window to compute the pixel-per-ms rate, tracing back through sample points to find which fall within range before breaking the loop.\n\nWait, the pointerup has the same x-position as the last move sample, so velocity computes to zero since no actual movement happened in that final interval—this is a harness timing artifact where the finger pauses before lifting. I should compute velocity from move samples only, using a window ending at the last move rather than the up event, and treat long gaps between last move and lift as a deliberate hold (v=0). But even with a proper 100ms window of move samples, the harness's slow sampling rate produces a velocity below my flick threshold, so I'm reconsidering whether 0.45 px/ms is too strict and whether something closer to 0.3 px/ms matches real-world flick thresholds better.\n\nFor the test itself, I'll make the flick move 120px across 3 samples at roughly 0.8 px/ms, which is fast enough to register as a flick while still covering less than 40% of the width—confirming it's a legitimate short flick rather than a full drag.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19f01841c001brIRtG679GJrrG","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19f0149a9001SyheAuI776BG2B"}}
