{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793669154207,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"toolu_011pw9oZuFrMpzD1u5ALm3ce","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd ~/openfang-build/repo/crates/openfang-api/static/js && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='app.js'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''      this.$watch('$store.app.sideOpen', function(isOpen) {\n        self.handOffFocus(isOpen);'''\nnew='''      this.$watch('$store.app.sideOpen', function(isOpen) {\n        if (isOpen) self.placeHeld();\n        self.handOffFocus(isOpen);'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''    // Keyboard users toggle with the same button:'''\nnew='''    // The menu button held above the open card sits exactly where the page's\n    // own menu button is, so a second tap in the same spot closes the card.\n    // When that spot would land on the card's wordmark (a mid-width desktop\n    // window), it takes the header's leading slot instead (the CSS default).\n    placeHeld() {\n      var held = document.querySelector('.sd-toggle');\n      if (!held) return;\n      held.style.left = '';\n      held.style.top = '';\n      var page = Array.prototype.find.call(document.querySelectorAll('.stax-menu-btn'), function(b) {\n        return b !== held && b.offsetParent !== null;\n      });\n      var brand = this.$el.querySelector('.sd-brand');\n      if (!page || !brand) return;\n      var r = page.getBoundingClientRect();\n      var brandRight = brand.getBoundingClientRect().right - this.$el.getBoundingClientRect().left;\n      if (r.left <= 12 || r.left >= brandRight + 8) {\n        held.style.left = Math.round(r.left) + 'px';\n        held.style.top = Math.round(r.top) + 'px';\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Keyboard users toggle with the same button:'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''          if (g.mode === 'open') self.collapseAll();       // the card arrives as it always opens'''\nnew='''          if (g.mode === 'open') { self.collapseAll(); self.placeHeld(); }  // the card arrives as it always opens'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode -e \"new Function(require('fs').readFileSync('app.js','utf8'))\" && echo OK"},"output":"OK\n","metadata":{"output":"OK\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd ~/openfang-build/repo/crates/openfang-api/static/js && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='app.js'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''      this.$watch('$store.app.sideOpen', function(isOpen) {\n        self.handOffFocus(isOpen);'''\nnew='''      this.$watch('$store.app.sideOpen', function(isOpen) {\n        if (isOpen) self.placeHeld();\n        self.handOffFocus(isOpen);'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''    // Keyboard users toggle with the same button:'''\nnew='''    // The menu button held above the open card sits exactly where the page's\n    // own menu button is, so a second tap in the same spot closes the card.\n    // When that spot would land on the card's wordmark (a mid-width desktop\n    // window), it takes the header's leading slot instead (the CSS default).\n    placeHeld() {\n      var held = document.querySelector('.sd-toggle');\n      if (!held) return;\n      held.style.left = '';\n      held.style.top = '';\n      var page = Array.prototype.find.call(document.querySelectorAll('.stax-menu-btn'), function(b) {\n        return b !== held && b.offsetParent !== null;\n      });\n      var brand = this.$el.querySelector('.sd-brand');\n      if (!page || !brand) return;\n      var r = page.getBoundingClientRect();\n      var brandRight = brand.getBoundingClientRect().right - this.$el.getBoundingClientRect().left;\n      if (r.left <= 12 || r.left >= brandRight + 8) {\n        held.style.left = Math.round(r.left) + 'px';\n        held.style.top = Math.round(r.top) + 'px';\n      }\n    },\n\n    // Keyboard users toggle with the same button:'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold='''          if (g.mode === 'open') self.collapseAll();       // the card arrives as it always opens'''\nnew='''          if (g.mode === 'open') { self.collapseAll(); self.placeHeld(); }  // the card arrives as it always opens'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode -e \"new Function(require('fs').readFileSync('app.js','utf8'))\" && echo OK","time":{"start":1793669154129,"end":1793669154205}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"On desktop, the hamburger toggle at that same page coordinate ends up covered by the open drawer card, so my \"same spot\" test doesn't actually hold there since the toggle lives in the drawer header slot instead. I need to check whether tapping that same location again still closes it properly given the card now occupies that space.\n\nI'll go with measuring the visible page hamburger's position and placing the twin there on open, falling back to the default leading slot if that spot would overlap the brand/wordmark area — computing the brand's right edge to decide when to fall back.\n\nI'll call placeHeld during the drawer's open watcher and at drag engagement time, keeping it as a shared method on staxDrawer rather than duplicating logic; resize-while-open can be skipped for now. For desktop, mouse interaction naturally handles scrolling inside the card, so no extra work needed there.\n\nI'm also noticing a desktop tap test failure since elementFromPoint at that coordinate hits the inert region instead of the intended target — I need to update the test to tap the twin's actual rect and the page spot afterward.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19f03374b001FaSIV4Ag3jTDHG","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19f02e398001KfN8nMJU3WWn3C"}}
