el=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/shawnlowe/openfang-build/repo/crates/openfang-api/static/index_head.html","text":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>OpenFang Dashboard</title>\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/x-icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" href=\"/logo.png\">\n<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/manifest.json\" crossorigin=\"use-credentials\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#146e68\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":14,"totalLines":14,"truncated":false}},"title":"crates/openfang-api/static/index_head.html","time":{"start":1793669346628,"end":1793669346643}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The image holds up fine at 180px, staying transparent. I'm weighing file size tradeoffs for delivery — the original is too large for inline base64, so I'm considering downscaling to around 512px to balance quality across different device pixel ratios while keeping payload size reasonable.\n\nI decide to ship a 512px lossless resample as the delivery copy, keeping the original PNG and SVG in static/brand/ for provenance, but skipping the unused idle jpg entirely to avoid repo bloat. I'm embedding the resampled PNG as base64 in webchat.rs, wiring it into the CSS background-image via include_str!...\n\nStill, I want to use the avatar SVG as an inline sprite symbol, embedding its viewBox and inner group as-is, and I need to think through how its presentation attributes (fill/stroke) interact with the `.sd-ico` CSS class that sets stroke and currentColor on usage.\n\nI'll put fill=\"none\" directly on the symbol element itself, mirroring the root svg attribute, which keeps the presentation attributes properly inherited into the clone. The dock icon can reuse the same symbol via a simple use reference at 26px, and the dark-mode outline color should still read fine against the dock background since the skull fill stays cream. For the home avatar, the reaper sits on a teal circle at 62% scale, which should work well visually.\n\nRereading the brief, \"replaces the arrow orb\" suggests the whole teal orb is swapped out for the reaper, not just the arrow inside it — so for avatars I should drop the teal fill entirely and use a subtler surface-tone circle background instead, while for the drawer brand tile the teal square stays and only the arrow glyph itself gets replaced by the reaper.\n\nSame tinted-circle treatment applies to the home avatar and drawer brand tile. I'll swap the sign-in arrow, sidebar logo, and \"Ask Stax\" chips to use the reaper sprite at various sizes, and replace the mascot centerpiece SVG with a styled span element representing the art.\n\nI'm sizing the mascot art down to 180px on phone and 196px on desktop, stripping out the now-unused halo/ring CSS and keyframes, but keeping a subtle fade-up entrance animation gated behind reduced-motion checks. The sd-mark symbol stays in the sprite for use on the Advanced page's identity line, paired with \"StaxCloud\" text.\n\nNow I need to check whether the favicon can be swapped for a data URI SVG of the avatar, so I'm looking at the index_head markup.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxjbGF1ZGUtb24tYXdzIn0"}]}},"id":"prt_19f063534001zW8ObD7NWFezUN","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","messageID":"msg_19f05bc8b001hN59BDKGMr9N6c"}}
