{"type":"text","timestamp":1793671100919,"sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","part":{"id":"prt_19f20c565001Ypy539lVuW1En0","messageID":"msg_19f2095c4001gZ7nIynJVAH7Br","sessionID":"ses_e6107b5a3ffeOiP9j8PWmY0U9w","type":"text","text":"Both parts of Round 3 are built and committed as two local commits on stax-ux, and the final release binary is running on staging. Every gesture in the brief passed in my browser runs at 390×844 and desktop, in dark and light. Two things did not come out clean: the full clippy lint fails in a file outside this round's scope, and the phone's home-screen icon is still the old OpenFang one.\n\n- **Commits:** `d0d6789` (Part A) and `f7bd958` (Part B). Nothing was deployed or pushed.\n- **Build:** the release build passed. The binary hash starts `2b64573c7366e7ca`.\n- **Tests:** all `openfang-api` tests pass.\n- **Staging:** running from `/tmp/opencode/r3/openfang-r3` on `127.0.0.1:4396`. Screenshots are in `~/openfang-build/round3-shots/` (89 files).\n\n## Part A — the side card moves like a card\n- **X removed:** the drawer header now holds only the reaper tile, \"StaxCloud\" and \"Fargo Tattoo\". The X icon was deleted from the sprite, and a scan found no close button or X in the drawer.\n- **Hamburger toggle:** every surface's three-line button opens the card. When the card is open, the same button sits above it at the spot you tapped, so tapping it again closes it.\n  - On the phone it lands within 2px of where it was.\n  - On desktop it stays where the page's button was. If that spot would cover the wordmark, it moves to the left end of the header.\n- **Gestures:** Pointer Events, with only transform and opacity changing while your finger is down. The open/close threshold is 40% of the card's width; a quick flick decides on its own.\n  - Vertical drags are released at the first clear movement, so scrolling isn't taken over.\n  - With reduced motion turned on there is no dragging; the button, tapping the dimmed page and ESC still work.\n  - The drawer's insides are unchanged.\n\n**Gesture results (touch on phone, mouse on desktop; all pass in all four combinations):**\n- The hamburger opens and closes, both by script and by a real tap or click.\n- An edge drag to 25% snaps shut; an edge drag to 60% opens.\n- A flick from the edge covering 33% of the width opens.\n- Dragging the card left 20% leaves it open; dragging 55% closes it.\n- A quick 33% left swipe on the card closes it.\n- Dragging the dimmed page left closes it; tapping it closes it.\n- A drag starting at x=60 does not open the card.\n- A vertical drag inside the edge zone does not open the card.\n- Vertical scrolling inside the open card works (scrolled 171px).\n- Sections are closed each time the card opens; ESC closes it.\n- Mid-drag captures are saved as `*-a2`, `*-a3` and `*-a5`.\n\n**What the harness could not prove:**\n- It sends synthetic touches through headless Chrome, not a real finger, so the feel of the follow and flick speed needs your phone.\n- On Android with gesture navigation, the system \"back\" swipe uses the same left-edge strip. The phone may take some edge swipes before the page sees them; the web page can't prevent this.\n- In the harness, desktop mouse drags can't scroll, so the \"still scrolls\" check only counts on the phone.\n\n## Part B — the grim reaper is the brand\n- **Reaper avatar:** `stax-avatar.svg` is copied verbatim into the single icon sprite. It replaces the arrow on:\n  - the drawer brand tile and the TEAM Stax row\n  - the Home header and Stax's message avatars in the conversation\n  - the Stax card\n  - the dock's Stax tab (the old mascot-head icon was removed)\n  - the \"Ask Stax\" chips in Settings and Connections, since they also represent Stax\n\n  Work, Boards, Leads, Channels and the drawer row icons are untouched.\n- **Home centerpiece:** I shipped **`stax-mascot-phone.png`**. It holds up at 180px and has a transparent background. The idle JPG has a white background, which would show as a white box in dark mode. It renders at 180px on phone and 196px on desktop; the status pill, greeting, button and composer did not move.\n- **How the mascot is served:** I resized it to 512px and embedded it in the page from `webchat.rs`, so no new route was needed. That adds about 286KB to every page load. Embedding the original 1MB file instead would add about 1.35MB per load, since the page isn't cached. The canonical original and the avatar are in `static/brand/` unchanged (hashes match).\n- **Sign-in:** the reaper replaces the arrow tile.\n- **Favicon:** it was a static asset, so `index_head.html` now points the browser-tab icon at the reaper avatar. The old `favicon.ico` and `logo.png` files are untouched.\n- **The arrow mark:** it now appears only on the System > Advanced page, as a small identity line (\"StaxCloud\" plus the version). No standalone arrow file existed in the tree; it only ever lived inside the page markup.\n\n## Non-regression (staging binary, all four combinations)\n- Drawer sections all start closed, Owner is the last block in the one scroll, and there is no tiles strip.\n- Settings and Connections are plain lists; the System module dock works.\n- Vocabulary scans on Settings and Connections are clean. Advanced shows its machinery words, as allowed.\n- The sprite has 21 symbols and no broken references.\n- **Console:** no JavaScript errors or warnings. The only red lines are network ones, the same as Round 2's baseline: 401s on the sign-in screen before login, and 404s for the morning brief and setup records that don't exist yet on a fresh staging home.\n\n## Found and fixed\n- The sign-in card had a dark background in light mode, with dark text on it. It now uses the theme's surface color.\n- On phones, a tap could leave the held hamburger showing a grey hover box. Hover styling now applies only to devices that actually hover.\n- The desktop header-spacing tweak is a Part A change, but it ended up in the Part B commit.\n\n## Found, not fixed\n- **Clippy:** `cargo clippy -p openfang-api --all-targets -D warnings` fails on `double_must_use` in `crates/openfang-types/src/memory.rs`. That is the newer lint tripping over existing code in `openfang-types`, which is outside the files this round may touch.\n- **Home-screen icon:** the installable-app manifest still uses `/logo.png` (the OpenFang snake). Changing it needs a new raster file and a route, which the brief rules out. For the same reason, the browser tab title is still \"OpenFang Dashboard\".","time":{"start":1793671087461,"end":1793671100914}}}
